# OpenRouter Rules

OpenRouter is used **only** as an internal peak-hour fallback provider for DeepSeek models. It is not advertised as a user-selectable provider; Cursor aliases map to direct providers and the gateway reroutes to OpenRouter upstream IDs during peak hours.

## HARD RULE: OpenRouter is peak-only

OpenRouter may **only** be used while the target provider (DeepSeek) is in peak
billing (per-provider windows; `DISCURSIVE_FORCE_PEAK` counts as peak). At all
other times every path — peak reroute, subagent/router downgrade, glm-4.7 lane
overflow, Z.AI lane overflow, sticky fallback, Z.AI 429-quota fallback, and the
compression worker — uses the **real** provider's real model:

- Downgrades/overflows → `deepseek-v4-flash` (small) / `deepseek-v4-pro` (big)
- The compressor always runs direct DeepSeek flash
- Subagent router candidates are exactly `deepseek-v4-flash` / `deepseek-v4-pro`

Enforcement is threefold:
1. Central mapping: `Server.fallbackTargetFor(model, requestID)` in
   `internal/gateway/fallback.go` is the only path that substitutes OpenRouter
   ids (gated on peak + OR key). All fallback callers go through it.
2. Send-time guard: `Server.isPeakAllowedOpenRouter` in `peakguard.go` runs
   just before key/URL resolution; off-peak OpenRouter models are corrected
   back to the real DeepSeek model and logged at ERROR.
3. Tests: `TestOpenRouterOnlyDuringPeak` asserts every fallback/override path
   returns a non-OpenRouter model when peak is off, and that the guard
   corrects OR ids off-peak and keeps them under `DISCURSIVE_FORCE_PEAK`.

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ----- | ---- | ----- |
| OpenRouter charged/used outside peak windows | A fallback/override path hardcoded an OR id (pre-0.7.2 behavior) | Route through `fallbackTargetFor`; never hardcode OR ids at call sites |
| `openrouter_guard: off-peak OpenRouter usage blocked` in logs | A new path produced an OR model off-peak; the guard corrected it | Find the producer and route it through `fallbackTargetFor` |

## Models

| Upstream id                        | Fallback target | Size class |
| ---------------------------------- | --------------- | ---------- |
| `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731`  | small/flash     | small      |
| `deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-0813`    | big/pro         | big        |

Peak reroute mapping (non-downgraded traffic only):
- `deepseek-v4-pro`, `glm-5.3`, `kimi-k3` → `deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-0813`
- everything else (`deepseek-v4-flash`, `glm-4.7`, `kimi-k2.7-code`, `thaura`) → `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731`

All subagent/router downgrades, lane-full overflows, and Z.AI 429-quota
fallbacks go through `Server.fallbackTargetFor` (fallback.go): real DeepSeek
flash/pro off-peak, OpenRouter equivalents only while DeepSeek is in peak and
an OR key exists. The compression worker always runs direct
`deepseek-v4-flash`.

## API key

- Key field: `openRouterKeyEncrypted` in `config.AppSettings`
- Set via: `discursive set --openrouter-key <key>` or `--openrouter-key` flag on `init`
- Retrieved via: `settings.GetOpenRouterKey(dataRoot)` in gateway/server.go
- OpenRouter is optional — if no key is configured, peak traffic falls through to the direct provider (pay peak), zero downtime

